                        "review": "TLDR: DO NOT PAY FULL PRICE – this is a tech demo. An interesting one with a decent mechanic, but there is no way they should be allowed to call this complete. \n\n[b][u]General Thoughts/Overview:[/u][/b]\nLucifer Within Us (LWU) is a short but interesting detective game, who’s primary mechanic involves picking apart testimonies on a timeline. \nWe are Ada, an exorcist. Apparently that makes us also the detective, as humans only commit crimes while possessed in this world. It’s been 111 years since the last murder, and oh BOY are we about to see that change. \nSo we find ourselves investigating environments and people, using every clue on every other clue, telling people they’re liars about everything, breaking into their minds to learn about them, and constructing insane loops to see who we can accuse in this introduction to a mechanic disguising itself as a game. \n\n[b][u]Pros:[/u][/b]\n[list][*] The mechanic is quite novel and I would have loved to see a full game of it.\n[*] The puzzles are straightforward, you have all the information, and if you don’t then you can bully everyone involved until you DO have all the information. \n[*] Super interesting premise combined with stories which fit the theme. It’s clear someone had a good idea, but didn’t follow it all the way through. \n[/list]\n\n[b][u]Cons:[/u][/b]\n[list][*] This is a tech demo, or proof of concept, not a game. I completed it AND did a 100% run in <4 hours. This is an introduction to the mechanics and world at best.  \n[*] LWU is so easy, and even if it wasn’t it’s simple to brute force and has no consequences for failure, removing all stakes and neutering a large part of what could give it deeper meaning.  \n[*] Other than the mechanic itself, nothing about this game is memorable. There isn’t enough time to build up to a decent payoff, or develop the characters into anything beyond archetypes. \n[/list]\n\n[b][u]Suggested improvements:[/u][/b]\n[list][*] A better way of combining evidence or setting up a timeline to challenge inconsistencies would help. I found myself trying to work out WHICH section I needed to call out to get the inconsistency I’d already seen. \n[*] Grey out options already asked, so I can track who I have asked what. \n[*] Rewrite the ending so it doesn’t feel like an ad for a non-existent game. \n[/list]\n\n\n[b][u]Overall Recommendation:[/u][/b]\nOverall I say this is an “on sale only.” This is categorically not worth full price, and it goes for three quid, which is still touch and go for its value.\n\nIf you like detective games, this is just built for you, and you should absolutely give it a whirl. Other than that, I recommend this to people who enjoy simple puzzle games and people looking for something unique to try. \n\nI don’t recommend this to people looking for a full on experience. This is shorter than my temper and you can 100% it in a single evening. I don’t recommend this to people who dislike logic deduction, and I don’t recommend it to people looking for something challenging.\n\nAll in all I enjoyed my brief time with LWU, but I can’t believe they’re allowed to get away with producing what amounts to a demo and slapping a full on price tag on it. \n\n[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/44852412/]My curator page[/url] with reviews by genre. In case you want to find more games, or even reviews, like this one.",
